{"title":"Four Fours","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Four Fours</b> is a mathematical puzzle where whole numbers are obtained using mathematical symbols and the number <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=4\" title=\"4\">four</a> four times. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebfee14521db2f55deb24b9807547378373bd93d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 - 4 + 4 - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/d/c6d279ebcd109d80e93656a9cd33243223b0c2ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4 - 4) \\times 4 \\times 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>There are many variants of Four Fours, like using other numbers instead of four, and different variants may allow different operations and combining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s (e.g. having <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/7764bd85172e8a58e2782f36b98c64be8ab71351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44 - 4 - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/4/3041c599da18e430aa7de4fa76485214c7293ebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$444 / 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"47\" height=\"20\" />)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours/0\" title=\"Four Fours/0\">Four Fours/0</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours/1\" title=\"Four Fours/1\">Four Fours/1</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours/2\" title=\"Four Fours/2\">Four Fours/2</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours/3\" title=\"Four Fours/3\">Four Fours/3</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours/4\" title=\"Four Fours/4\">Four Fours/4</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours/5\" title=\"Four Fours/5\">Four Fours/5</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours/6\" title=\"Four Fours/6\">Four Fours/6</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours/7\" title=\"Four Fours/7\">Four Fours/7</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours/8\" title=\"Four Fours/8\">Four Fours/8</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours/9\" title=\"Four Fours/9\">Four Fours/9</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours/10\" title=\"Four Fours/10\">Four Fours/10</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours/11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Four Fours/11 (page does not exist)\">Four Fours/11</a></li></ul>\n<p>For solutions above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, see <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Special%3APrefixIndex&amp;prefix=Four+Fours%2F&amp;namespace=0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Symbols_Used\">Symbols Used</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four_Fours&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Symbols Used\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/2536afe4a66052cb0b42654bf2ac67327027527c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$!x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, representing the subfactorial of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/6/f7698a3f9be9c1b3fe122d76f0ab6a65b8ebc627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$!4 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36edacaf2ec3d06fb117f981d12f42cdee6cf940.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />, representing the gamma function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> (e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d7d0ab2d5aeb247896b74e82987360eca4a08e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma(4) = 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/2950e3accfad26309bf1ecf6947061171fd2797f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x!$\" width=\"14\" height=\"13\" />, representing the factorial of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a002511f7c413485389dc4691555da8b6aec0ffc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4! = 4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"186\" height=\"16\" />)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de1a36d69a7028480a87b712a7141c651398a06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, representing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> percent (e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85f957e21dd5b11e993c589756f0b0f09f9347e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\% = 0.04$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f9af910fe749481919573c0dd2b132118f19d19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^y$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, representing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> power (e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1dd48fefcd101384d02c7d79ce469dd15582e079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^4 = 256$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/4805dddb4e6911989af8be91da334b5ba2054757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />, representing the square root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> (e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/625885b53be76678065cd8de7fa159e040ebe848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{4} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />)\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018084831\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 111/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4570/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37236:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018084831 and revision id 287533. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}